Build 028, from the 026/027 console runs:
- Images of 8 MiB or more (EDEN_NX2_DEDICATED_IMAGE_MIB, /data/eden-nx2/dedicated-image-mib.txt, 0 = off)
  get their own memory allocation. An image evicted from one of VMA's shared 64 MiB blocks leaves a hole
  the pool only gets back once the whole block is empty; at the 026/027 crashes the device-local blocks
  held 545-907 MiB of holes while the game's own memory found 1 MiB free. Dedicated memory goes back to
  the pool when the image is freed, so the texture collector's evictions under pressure reach the pool.
- The draw trace (trace-draws.txt) logs each traced draw's depth and colour targets with their layers,
  the render-target layer register (0x15CC, not read by the texture cache) and viewport 0: the nearest
  shadow cascade (layer 0 of a 3-layer depth array) was never written in the 026/027 captures.
- The frame capture keeps small images too (last 96 drawn): the exposure reduction's 16x8..16x1 targets.

